{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes","id":557831,"title":"My variants for clan banes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-16T21:36:01-07:00","id":557831,"title":"My variants for clan banes","content":"Now I'm thinking upon some new format for clan banes. What I've got in the 2nd ed, seems to me the move in the right direction, but the result is not what I quite like. So, what about, for example these:<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue. The Curse of the Ambition.</b><br /> The Beast of Ventrue is the embodiment of great Ambition. Ventrue always win. Ventrue always get what they want. Choose one of your Aspirations. It becomes the main goal to you. After the chapter in which you did nothing to fulfill it, roll Humanity. If you fail the roll, take the Deprived condition.<br /> On the other side, if you fulfill (or achieve great success on the way to fulfill) your Aspiration, roll Blood Potency. You gain [successes] Willpower points (but not more you\u2019ve spent).<br /> <br /> <b>Daeva. The Curse of the Passion.</b><br /> The Beast of Daeva is the Beast of Passion and desire. There\u2019s never enough for Daeva, never too far. When you fulfill any of your Aspirations, roll Humanity. If you fail the roll, take the Hedonistic condition.<br /> On the other side, when you take a new Aspiration, roll Blood Potency. You gain [successes] Willpower points (but not more you\u2019ve spent).<br /> ---<br /> [Hedonistic Condition]<br /> What you,ve got is not enough for you. You want more. You cannot resolve your Aspiration until you resolute this Condition.<br /> Possible sources: The Curse of the Passion.<br /> Beat: each time your Aspiration becomes breaking point for you, get a beat.<br /> Resolution: fail the breaking point for resolving your Aspiration.<br /> <br /> I've not done other clan banes yet, but the idea is to use Humanity, Blood potency and some other plot-oriented traits (aspirations, touchstones, mask and dirge). And also make it a source of Willpower and Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-17-2015, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T22:44:14-07:00","id":557913,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea to have the clan banes be clan blessings half the time.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't personally run anything off aspirations. Aspirations can be anything from &quot;Go hunting&quot; to &quot;bloodbond the President,&quot; so it's really way too easy to manipulate your bane this way. This is mostly a concern for Ventrue, who get bonuses for fulfilling aspirations and no penalties. Daeva get both rewards and penalties, so there's less motivation to game it, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T23:11:52-07:00","id":557926,"title":"","content":"Mania, well, Ventrue and Daeva are the most desire-driven clans of all, so that was the point in using aspirations. As for Daeva this variant can turn any aspiration into the long-term source of beats, for risking Humanity, but character is also motivated to changing aspirations. As for Ventrue, I know. My variant seems not so harsh as should be. May be, key Aspiration should be for them the long-term one and rolls for Deprivation should be done every session he didn't actually ACHIEVE it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-17-2015, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T05:42:23-07:00","id":558120,"title":"","content":"While aspirations can make sense for Ventrue, I don't think its thematically appropriate for the Deava. Aspirations aren't about emotions or desire - they can be very cold blooded, and the idea is to emphasize the passion of the clan, isn't it?<br /> <br /> That said, I also like linking them to Humanity - I like how the banes get worse as you get more monstrous.<br /> <br /> EDIT - fixed first line. Forgot to say I was talking about the daeva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-17-2015, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:04:40-07:00","id":558143,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget that aspirations can be a totally Out of Char thing. For example &quot;My Ghoul is slain&quot;, &quot;meet a changeling&quot; (when the character doesn't know they exist at all, but the player knows), &quot;I am captured by my enemy&quot; are all totally valid aspirations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:48:28-07:00","id":558200,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! <br /> <br /> Well, maybe not necessarily an aspiration, or at least an OC aspiration. But maybe they have to pick a goal. I also like the idea that it can also be blessing as well. My only concern is that it may be exploited (I mention this in the Daeva section as I feel it should be related to their blood dolls. Depending on the character, they can easily succeed in these areas and reap the benefits)<br /> <br /> For Ventrue, something that will help propel their 'career' or plans. Probably mostly related to the 'Game of Thrones' (Sadly, I've been using that term since before the show, can't say about the books as I don't know when they were written). Whether it is them trying to become Prince of the city, or a different city. Trying to get ahead in their local covenant or clan. Something along those lines. (ex. I want to attain the rank of Seneschal in the local city. I want to become my clan's Primogen). <br /> <br /> For Daeva, although might be easy to exploit, it being related to something personal for them. Although it should be more complicate then just &quot;I want to acquire a new blood doll&quot;. Although you could maybe make them more specific. 'I want to acquire a blood doll who is close to the Ventrue Primogen&quot;. Or maybe... Hmm, not sure really. I feel like, if going this route, it should be related to blood dolls still. If not obtaining, then retaining. Or spoiling them perhaps. 'I want to buy my blood dolls a communial house for them to live in&quot;. &quot;I want to help my blood doll excel in her career at the local newspaper&quot;.. Still not sure about this one.<br /> <br /> I don't really remember the banes for others. So can't comment too much on them (been quite awhile since I've flipped through 2E (when it was still B&amp;S)). 'Tis just thoughts! <br /> <br /> Opinion?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:54:22-07:00","id":558431,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof\">Krzyzstof</a></b>, yep, you've grasped the idea.<br /> <br /> The problem as I see it is that while setting tells us about the clan psychology, dictated by the Beast, the system doesn't really encourage us to do it... or doesn't make us too. As for my opinion, it should encourage and make both. It pretty well represents the Beast - the Beast's urges that dictate some way of behavior or lure into it. And that's not even the choice of the character - and never should be! It's a Curse!<br /> <br /> Ventrue are ambitious. Why? Because their Beast is! It wants to subdue, to dominate. It gives them the perfect instrument for it - Dominate discopline - and wants it used to fulfill its urges. And it doesn't care if the Kindred themselves want it or not. If they do so he rewards them. If they don't... it can turn their unlives into hell.<br /> <br /> Daeva are passionate. That's also their Beast that drives them to the edge of sencitive experience. Never enough. Never too far.<br /> <br /> Gangrel are feral. Their Beast is concerned hunt and survival, it doesn't care of anything else.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu are monstrous. Their Beast wants to bring horror and fear into the world.<br /> <br /> Mekhet... well, their Beast is the most complicated. A bit Lovecraftian, a bit God-Machine-like (remember frenzy described in &quot;Shadow in the Dark&quot;?).<br /> <br /> The point IMO is to make Curse dictating behavior. But not too often, for the characters could do other things. But often enough to make them remember that they're not blessed. They're cursed.<br /> <br /> By the way, it's a good idea to make 'blessing' side of Clan Banes be connected with breaking points - some kind of 'Devil's Contract'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T11:20:32-07:00","id":558477,"title":"","content":"Hmm.. I think that moving characters to act with their clan psychology would work better by letting them regain a point of willpower (or even a complete refill) whenever they act in accordance to their clan archetype, either instead of either mask or dirge, or in addition to both of them instead of using the clan banes. E.g. Ventrue regain Willpower when one of their plans moves forwards, Daeva when they indulge their base desires, Gangrel when they succeed without using 'weak' methods (or something else better), Nosferatu and Mekhet something that I'm not sure about yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:29:05-07:00","id":558730,"title":"","content":"How about making it a <i>real</i> gamble?<br /> <br /> You can recover Willpower if you do something in line with your Clan stereotype. Daeva seduce someone to feed; the Ventrue advances their plans, a Gangrel lashes out savagely.<br /> <br /> If you go overboard and let the Beast &quot;play&quot;, you get a Willpower point <i>and one Vitae</i>. Go on - indulge in being a monster.<br /> <br /> Actually... what if each Clan could &quot;partake&quot; in certain behaviours without suffering a Humanity breaking point? It might take a rejigger of Humanity, but that would be interesting - the whole Lucy thing and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T03:53:04-07:00","id":561764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=558431#post558431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem as I see it is that while setting tells us about the clan psychology, dictated by the Beast, the system doesn't really encourage us to do it... or doesn't make us too. As for my opinion, it should encourage and make both. It pretty well represents the Beast - the Beast's urges that dictate some way of behavior or lure into it. And that's not even the choice of the character - and never should be! It's a Curse!<br /> <br /> Ventrue are ambitious. Why? Because their Beast is! It wants to subdue, to dominate. It gives them the perfect instrument for it - Dominate discopline - and wants it used to fulfill its urges. And it doesn't care if the Kindred themselves want it or not. If they do so he rewards them. If they don't... it can turn their unlives into hell.<br /> <br /> Daeva are passionate. That's also their Beast that drives them to the edge of sencitive experience. Never enough. Never too far.<br /> <br /> Gangrel are feral. Their Beast is concerned hunt and survival, it doesn't care of anything else.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu are monstrous. Their Beast wants to bring horror and fear into the world.<br /> <br /> Mekhet... well, their Beast is the most complicated. A bit Lovecraftian, a bit God-Machine-like (remember frenzy described in &quot;Shadow in the Dark&quot;?).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a side note, I have always linked the psychology of the clans with the way they feed:<br /> <br /> Daeva. It's the act of feeding as an act of seduction. It's a metaphor for the sexual act. It's intimate. I'm the perversion of lust and love.<br /> <br /> Gangrel. It's the act of feeding as an act of consumption. It's feral and primal, it's basic. They are some predators out there and you are the fucking prey. I'm hungry and you are consumable.<br /> <br /> Mekhet. It's the act of feeding as an act of occult signifiance. It's alien, you may even never know that blood has be taken from you. And it's strange, unknown, the blood taken from you becoming the fuel of the undead form that I wear.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: It's the act of feeding as a monsruous act. Right, drinking blood is cannibalism, nothing more, nothing less. It's disgusting and horrible, and only monsters are capable of such thing. I'm eating a little of myself while drinking from you.<br /> <br /> Ventrue. It's the act of feeding as an act of domination. It's just a game of who is the dominant. See it as a tithe or as bullying, but I'm your better and feeding from you is the right things to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T16:01:57-07:00","id":562286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=561764#post561764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a side note, I have always linked the psychology of the clans with the way they feed:</div> </div> </div> </div>Resembles Auspices linked to the way they hunt. Great! This can be something to think of, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:52:01-07:00","id":563214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=561764#post561764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a side note, I have always linked the psychology of the clans with the way they feed:<br /> <br /> Daeva. It's the act of feeding as an act of seduction. It's a metaphor for the sexual act. It's intimate. I'm the perversion of lust and love.<br /> <br /> Gangrel. It's the act of feeding as an act of consumption. It's feral and primal, it's basic. They are some predators out there and you are the fucking prey. I'm hungry and you are consumable.<br /> <br /> Mekhet. It's the act of feeding as an act of occult signifiance. It's alien, you may even never know that blood has be taken from you. And it's strange, unknown, the blood taken from you becoming the fuel of the undead form that I wear.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: It's the act of feeding as a monsruous act. Right, drinking blood is cannibalism, nothing more, nothing less. It's disgusting and horrible, and only monsters are capable of such thing. I'm eating a little of myself while drinking from you.<br /> <br /> Ventrue. It's the act of feeding as an act of domination. It's just a game of who is the dominant. See it as a tithe or as bullying, but I'm your better and feeding from you is the right things to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. I've passed it on to the players as food for thought. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","user":"Corrigan","date":". 06-21-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:03:22-07:00","id":563469,"title":"","content":"While it's interesting to think about in broad strokes, I wouldn't want to mechanically enforce this &quot;clan psychology.&quot; People being less defined by their clan is something I really liked about VtR over VtM. Daeva don't have to be seductive, though they're more inclined towards it after Embrace. Mekhet might never get a dot of Obfuscate, so unseen feeding might never happen.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to view how the average vampire of each Clan may differ in broad strokes, but I get really wary when it comes to pigeonholing people into certain roles or behaviors or personalities based on their Clan. Clan isn't really something anybody chooses, so anyone could be a member of any Clan. A former rock star could end up Mekhet instead of Daeva, which might be what you'd expect. A total shut-in computer nerd could be Embraced by a Gangrel rather than a Nosferatu. A social worker that spends all their time trying to help others above themselves could end up Ventrue, etc, etc, etc. These aren't common cases, but I wouldn't want the mechanics to force them to act against who they are. These sorts of contradictions can make for really interesting characters.<br /> <br /> I also like the Beast being the one true unifying tribulation for Vampires, and what they build their Covenants around. That's more of a personal thing, though, and I won't fault anyone for having a different interpretation of the Beast.<br /> <br /> The Clan psychology thing above is kind of how I feel about the initial OP, too, but I didn't want the first reply to be something that was shooting down someone's ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:19:32-07:00","id":564691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=563469#post563469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's interesting to think about in broad strokes, I wouldn't want to mechanically enforce this &quot;clan psychology.&quot; People being less defined by their clan is something I really liked about VtR over VtM. Daeva don't have to be seductive, though they're more inclined towards it after Embrace. Mekhet might never get a dot of Obfuscate, so unseen feeding might never happen.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to view how the average vampire of each Clan may differ in broad strokes, but I get really wary when it comes to pigeonholing people into certain roles or behaviors or personalities based on their Clan. Clan isn't really something anybody chooses, so anyone could be a member of any Clan. A former rock star could end up Mekhet instead of Daeva, which might be what you'd expect. A total shut-in computer nerd could be Embraced by a Gangrel rather than a Nosferatu. A social worker that spends all their time trying to help others above themselves could end up Ventrue, etc, etc, etc. These aren't common cases, but I wouldn't want the mechanics to force them to act against who they are. These sorts of contradictions can make for really interesting characters.<br /> <br /> I also like the Beast being the one true unifying tribulation for Vampires, and what they build their Covenants around. That's more of a personal thing, though, and I won't fault anyone for having a different interpretation of the Beast.<br /> <br /> The Clan psychology thing above is kind of how I feel about the initial OP, too, but I didn't want the first reply to be something that was shooting down someone's ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that there should be flexibility, I also think Clan should be more than a template for different sets of Disciplines. If the Mekhet embraces a rock star, how does the &quot;mekhet-ness&quot; manifest? How would he be different than if he'd been embraced by a Daeva? Figuring out the core of a clan helps to make the character more distinctive, IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T01:33:23-07:00","id":565092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=564691#post564691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree that there should be flexibility, I also think Clan should be more than a template for different sets of Disciplines. If the Mekhet embraces a rock star, how does the &quot;mekhet-ness&quot; manifest? How would he be different than if he'd been embraced by a Daeva? Figuring out the core of a clan helps to make the character more distinctive, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those things are exactly the different sets of Disciplines. Since most of first dot powers are now free, the character has all the incentive to be more mekhet-y, by using Auspex and knowing shit and using Obfuscate and hiding better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T04:20:34-07:00","id":565172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=565092#post565092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those things are exactly the different sets of Disciplines. Since most of first dot powers are now free, the character has all the incentive to be more mekhet-y, by using Auspex and knowing shit and using Obfuscate and hiding better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... I was thinking less of &quot;This is my deck and I am going to strategize to use the cards to the best advantage&quot; and more &quot;It's weird, that place in my chest where I used to feel everything, it's now cold and still and dark as the grave, but it when I should be mad or excited it just goes stiller and colder and it's like I'm watching through the eyes of a stranger. And when I'm hungry it's not a pang so much as a pull like a blackhole in my chest and it's pulling on my ribs and if I don't do this I'll implode so I'm sorry-but- [slurrrp]&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","user":"Corrigan","date":". 06-23-2015, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T05:46:28-07:00","id":565265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=565172#post565172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... I was thinking less of &quot;Theis is my deck and I am going to strategize to use the cards to the best advantage&quot; and more &quot;It's weird, that place in my chest where I used to feel everything, it's now cold and still and dark as the grave, but it when I should be mad or excited it just goes stiller and colder and it's like I'm watching through the eyes of a stranger. And when I'm hungry it's not a pang so much as a pull like a blackhole in my chest and it's pulling on my ribs and if I don't do this I'll implode so I'm sorry-but- [slurrrp]&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only true if you exclude the disciplines into some offhand entity of &quot;this is my supernatural powers. This is my true self&quot;. I see disciplines more as extensions of the self (with the exclusion of sorceries and Coils).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:55:09-07:00","id":565354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=565265#post565265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's only true if you exclude the disciplines into some offhand entity of &quot;this is my supernatural powers. This is my true self&quot;. I see disciplines more as extensions of the self (with the exclusion of sorceries and Coils).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's how I see often see players looking at it. &quot;I'm a detective. My equipment list includes lockpicks, 9mm, knife, digital camera, and celerity.&quot; It's like &quot;hey, I spent points and powered up,&quot; but there's nothing of the inhuman in the psychological makeup of the character. I like things like the writeups upthread to give to players and say, &quot;Your character is part man, part monster. The monster wants the whole character. You will be playing from the mental frontlines. Run your playing through that filter.&quot; Otherwise, there's no flavor, only stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T11:19:14-07:00","id":565589,"title":"","content":"That's not just a player thing. There is fluff in the book that suggests (or flat out says, I don't recall) that Disciplines are channeling the Beast through the Blood and are learned instinctually, not really by choice. Players choose, sure, but that's a meta-conceit for the sake of playability. Like Bloodlines, they usually are not learned so much as a part of your very blood.<br /> <br /> The only exceptions are things you actually do learn, like the aforementioned Blood Sorceries or Coils and also the very few Disciplines that require drinking another person's Blood (all the clan-unique ones; majesty, nightmare, dominate, auspex, protean).<br /> <br /> They aren't really a part of your equipment list or stats any more than, say, Mask/Dirge/Touchstone are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T12:59:49-07:00","id":565677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=564691#post564691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that there should be flexibility, I also think Clan should be more than a template for different sets of Disciplines. If the Mekhet embraces a rock star, how does the &quot;mekhet-ness&quot; manifest? How would he be different than if he'd been embraced by a Daeva? Figuring out the core of a clan helps to make the character more distinctive, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Daeva embraces a rock star they start trying to be the best rock star ever.<br /> If a Mekhet embraces a rock star they become an underground hit, known by few but regarded as a genius.<br /> If a Ventrue embraces a rock star they start plotting to destroy their rivals. Probably with a concert and dominate.<br /> <br /> Can't really think of examples for the Gangrel and Nosferatu. But what if a Daeva had embraced that nerdy librarian, not a Mekhet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:59:43-07:00","id":565738,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; Can't really think of examples for the Gangrel and Nosferatu. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GeuW4Smf9PI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GeuW4Smf9PI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GeuW4Smf9PI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GeuW4Smf9PI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; But what if a Daeva had embraced that nerdy librarian, not a Mekhet? &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> You get Katherine Hepburn in Desk Set. Or Rachel Weisz in the Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T16:21:12-07:00","id":565837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=565589#post565589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players choose, sure, but that's a meta-conceit for the sake of playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>[JOKE]Easily solved! I already have a method of randomly generating a starting Lick, now you just need to roll randomly every time you would buy up a Discipline. Simples![/JOKE]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T01:31:26-07:00","id":566189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=565677#post565677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Daeva embraces a rock star they start trying to be the best rock star ever.<br /> If a Mekhet embraces a rock star they become an underground hit, known by few but regarded as a genius.<br /> If a Ventrue embraces a rock star they start plotting to destroy their rivals. Probably with a concert and dominate.<br /> <br /> Can't really think of examples for the Gangrel and Nosferatu. But what if a Daeva had embraced that nerdy librarian, not a Mekhet?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say if a rock star get's embraced, he does whatever the hell he used to do. But due to his discipline spread he starts doing it in more clan-like way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:14:01-07:00","id":566288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=566189#post566189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd say if a rock star get's embraced, he does whatever the hell he used to do. But due to his discipline spread he starts doing it in more clan-like way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. But that's also an external way of looking at things. Twins, one armed with a roll of duct tape and a screwdriver, the other with a hammer and pliers, will solve a mechanical problem in different ways based on their tool set. That's external. Nothing wrong with that at all, of course.<br /> <br /> Harry Dresden, the Dark Knight, and Sherlock Holmes will handle a mystery differently, not just because they have different tools at their disposal, but because they have very different worldviews, and fundementally different psyches. Jethro Gibbs and Rorschach can both sneak around and beat up people effectively, but their internal dialogues are worlds apart. <br /> <br /> I have to figure that the Beast, the Other, or whatever the vampire calls it, is a more powerful force in a person's psyche than an addiction or mania that a mortal might have. It's bigger than a mere dietary restriction or UV allergy. It's a palpable presence that influences everything the vampire does. Without that it just becomes a game about supercriminals IMO.<br /> <br /> I guess what I like to see are descriptions that highlight, not what a character can do, but what they are inside that makes them do what they do. That sort of detail adds a great deal to my interest in a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T08:33:13-07:00","id":566444,"title":"","content":"I kind of mix it between what Griatis and Corrigan said.<br /> <br /> I would think that while yes they tend to stick to methods similar to others of their clan, they add their own personal flare on it. Especially the younger the vampire, the more 'your way' you do it. The longer you've been 'alive', the more the beast starts to influence your actions.<br /> <br /> For example, if you were a big brawl-y biker gang member and for whatever reason a Mekhet took a liking to you and embraced you, I imagine for the first couple of years you are still going to be a big brawl-y biker thug who dabbles at stealth. If said thug lives long enough, I can see him using more stealth and less brute strength. So instead of breaking into a place and beating up his prey, he sneaks in and feeds on one. Yet if he were to be confronted by one, or a small handful, of enemies, I feel he would try to bash his way out instead of trying to sneak off (at least that's how I had most Mekhet portrayed. Would run from a fight they weren't certain they could win).<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I play it out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:20:21-07:00","id":566715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=566288#post566288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is true. But that's also an external way of looking at things. Twins, one armed with a roll of duct tape and a screwdriver, the other with a hammer and pliers, will solve a mechanical problem in different ways based on their tool set. That's external. Nothing wrong with that at all, of course.<br /> <br /> Harry Dresden, the Dark Knight, and Sherlock Holmes will handle a mystery differently, not just because they have different tools at their disposal, but because they have very different worldviews, and fundementally different psyches. Jethro Gibbs and Rorschach can both sneak around and beat up people effectively, but their internal dialogues are worlds apart.<br /> <br /> I have to figure that the Beast, the Other, or whatever the vampire calls it, is a more powerful force in a person's psyche than an addiction or mania that a mortal might have. It's bigger than a mere dietary restriction or UV allergy. It's a palpable presence that influences everything the vampire does. Without that it just becomes a game about supercriminals IMO.<br /> <br /> I guess what I like to see are descriptions that highlight, not what a character can do, but what they are inside that makes them do what they do. That sort of detail adds a great deal to my interest in a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;internal&quot; thing you mention is exactly what VtM more or less did, and its removal is one of my favorite changes in VtR. You are not defined by you clan. It does not change your personality. You are still you. What Clan does is give you newfound talents that encourage certain means of problem solving. That is, being a Daeva doesn't turn the nerdy girl into a party girl. It gives the nerdy girl a far greater aptitude for making everyone love her when she wants. She's not any more inclined to want it after being Embraced, but she is far more capable of getting it if she already wanted. The stereotypes Daeva have could just as easily be a mix of socially repressed people finally getting a shot at being the popular one as much as any inherent personality shift. Mixed with their Bane, of course, which sort of brings that tendency to an extreme.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, though. The reason I'm so fervent in this interpretation is probably less purely based on the books and more my personal views on the sanctity of the mind. If the Embrace changes someone's personality, then to me they die at the moment of the Embrace and something else wakes up as a vampire. It's no different from Buffy in that regard: just some other being possessing the dead person's corpse. Once again, it's a part of my worldview when it comes to identity and self, but an external force (the Beast) changing who someone is fundamentally is akin to that person being dead and something else walking in their place.<br /> <br /> Certainly a horrific interpretation, but not one I'm inclined to play. It's too bleak.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is a house rule thread, so house ruling an oWoD-style interpretation of the clans is totally valid. Given that it's valid for this thread's purpose, I should probably stop derailing. Apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:52:57-07:00","id":566760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=566189#post566189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd say if a rock star get's embraced, he does whatever the hell he used to do. But due to his discipline spread he starts doing it in more clan-like way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The night of the embrace? Yeah. Year afterwards he seems a bit less content to be in the limelight, and ten or twenty years later our Mekhet is just playing because he likes it or because it connects him to humanity. Maybe he used to play for the feel but now does it for the theory. Depending on how strongly he rejects his mekhet heritage he might be the member of the band that's crucial but overlooked, or he might even start his own bloodline of (ninja) scholar rocker vampires.<br /> <br /> I suggest Auspex, Celerity, Majesty and Obfuscate for the disciplines. No certain on bloodline gift, but the weakness might be a desperate need for companionship.<br /> <br /> I like nonstandard characters, but I don't think that clan should just be disciplines and clan banes. Some shadows are obvious, but the Shadows disappear with the light. Not all freaks are horrific, but every Freak is broken. Not all savages are stupid, but the Savages rely on instinct. Not all serpents are harmful, but the Serpents embody that excitement. Not all lords are noble, but the Lords are above others.<br /> <br /> It might not happen tonight. But it will happen one night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:05:17-07:00","id":568685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=558431#post558431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point IMO is to make Curse dictating behavior. But not too often, for the characters could do other things. But often enough to make them remember that they're not blessed. They're cursed.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, I asked about this question from a less mechanical, more role-playing angle recently in this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/531432-a-new-perspective\">trend</a>. It may or may not be useful in your project. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T18:26:13-07:00","id":575857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=566715#post566715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;internal&quot; thing you mention is exactly what VtM more or less did, and its removal is one of my favorite changes in VtR. You are not defined by you clan. It does not change your personality. You are still you. What Clan does is give you newfound talents that encourage certain means of problem solving. That is, being a Daeva doesn't turn the nerdy girl into a party girl. It gives the nerdy girl a far greater aptitude for making everyone love her when she wants. She's not any more inclined to want it after being Embraced, but she is far more capable of getting it if she already wanted. The stereotypes Daeva have could just as easily be a mix of socially repressed people finally getting a shot at being the popular one as much as any inherent personality shift. Mixed with their Bane, of course, which sort of brings that tendency to an extreme.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, though. The reason I'm so fervent in this interpretation is probably less purely based on the books and more my personal views on the sanctity of the mind. If the Embrace changes someone's personality, then to me they die at the moment of the Embrace and something else wakes up as a vampire. It's no different from Buffy in that regard: just some other being possessing the dead person's corpse. Once again, it's a part of my worldview when it comes to identity and self, but an external force (the Beast) changing who someone is fundamentally is akin to that person being dead and something else walking in their place.<br /> <br /> Certainly a horrific interpretation, but not one I'm inclined to play. It's too bleak.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, and our VtM characters rarely toed the line when it came to stereotypes. As far as the clan goes, I don\u2019t think it\u2019s a question of radical personality shift so much as an adjustment. The thing that keeps you moving and gives you superhuman powers shares your head with you. It requires a certain \u2026 accommodation and adjustment. I\u2019m of the opinion that this presence should have a distinct flavor depending on where it comes from \u2013 the clan relation. <br /> <br /> I really enjoyed the writeups in Danse Macabre (talking about beast, the blood, and the kiss in terms of the clan). In our game, the ghouls get a taste of that flavor. Like one of the Mekhet ghouls said, when discovered with the lights off: \u201cI like to sit in the dark. It\u2019s\u2026 soothing. Helps me think.\u201d<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T00:30:28-07:00","id":578371,"title":"","content":"Tough less worried about the &quot;soul death&quot; thing, I go with Maina. V:tM used precisely this kind of reasoning, and was a great setting.<br /> <br /> Until you notice that a majority of players will do the same characters. They change names, gender and dots, but a Toreador is like every other Toreador. You can go outside the stereotype, sure. But most players won't. I even saw a guy leaving the game table feeling insulted with the oppening speech of the ST, just because he said a Tremere Harpy would throw a party. The player stood up and walked away steaming and replying that &quot;Tremeres don't party. I will play with someone who knows the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ridiculous, but the more you give a stereotype to the clan, the more most players will stick to it as if it was sacred. And that because Masquerade never created any mechanical boon for &quot;roleplaying right&quot;. As good as V:tM was, the stereotype got old, even with thirteen clans, plus clan-like bloodlines, plus Antitribu. In a game with five it will kill the game in no time.<br /> <br /> The difference between &quot;external&quot; and &quot;internal&quot; is a perceived one. Everything you put a rule on is ultimately external until the player bring it into the character. Aspirations, Humanity and Touchstones, even Masks and Dirges aren't exceptions, by the way. The player, not the rules, will choose to bring this in-character or just use like a tool and them put aside. Even Disciplines can be brought in-character. Give someone the power of frightening the hell out of anyone else. It will be a matter of time before this power and its use start to inform that person about who she is.<br /> <br /> All that aside, I do find the Clan Banes less than satisfying and I'm not done with this thread. The idea of using Humanity is good, because it highlights the strugle Human vs Beast. But I wouldn't give any bonus, just more generic penalties. I also liked the idea of linking the Banes to other stuff in the character sheet, exactly because it highlights who your character is BEFORE the Beast, and THEM lets the Beast twist things.<br /> <br /> Daeva could be related to the Dirge, instead of Aspirations, or even to retaining the human Vice. Ventrue could be easily linked to the Mask, since it is a regal thing, I can see a Beast with dominating ambition parasiting the way the Mask works.<br /> <br /> Or another idea that occurred to me, they all could relate to the Predatory Aura. That is the way a vampire makes his Beast manifest, so why not? The Banes could affect the Predatory Aura in a failed Humanity roll to keep the Beast onthe line, or even trigger the Aura without the vampire decision on certain situations. Mix the two, and you could have a Ventrue that exibits the Aura when gaining willpower from his Mask, and a Daeva doing so with the Dirge. The Beast don't change the person directly, but when the person does certain things it cames from the bottom of the soul to the fore, snarling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:09:26-07:00","id":578907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557831-my-variants-for-clan-banes?p=578371#post578371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until you notice that a majority of players will do the same characters. They change names, gender and dots, but a Toreador is like every other Toreador. You can go outside the stereotype, sure. But most players won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best one is where players add their own stereotypes, the most common being 'Giovanni are in the mafia'. This is despite me defining them as 'in the money trade' every time, and having never seen a Giovanni mafisto as a PC (as it's 'too stereotypical').<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I even saw a guy leaving the game table feeling insulted with the oppening speech of the ST, just because he said a Tremere Harpy would throw a party. The player stood up and walked away steaming and replying that 'Tremeres don't party. I will play with someone who knows the game.' </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Of course Tremere throw parties. They'll just be very formal events compared even to the Ventrue (who'll skip formal occasionally as long as it's refined) and much more like a business party. How does this not fit in with the Tremere stereotype? I feel sorry for the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ridiculous, but the more you give a stereotype to the clan, the more most players will stick to it as if it was sacred. And that because Masquerade never created any mechanical boon for 'roleplaying right'. As good as V:tM was, the stereotype got old, even with thirteen clans, plus clan-like bloodlines, plus Antitribu. In a game with five it will kill the game in no time. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is why I prefer archetypal clans to stereotypical clans. In Requiem you have those archetypal clans which can fit a lot more, although I always find myself falling back on one stereotype (Mekhet scholar of the Ordo Dracul) when planning characters, to the point that when my friend finally runs his game I plan to play a Carthian Mekhet socialite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T14:52:11-07:00","id":579152,"title":"","content":"I, by myself, avoid stereotypes. My last Tremere avoided the clan at all costs and was much more at home with the city's Toreador. Even being an occultist even before the Embrace, she loved all sorts of classic art and was a romantic person. Not every member of a clan should fit with the stereotype, in truth I can easily imagine the majority skipping it in at least one aspect, even if almos all follow most of it.<br /> <br /> Either way, yeah, the player didn't even waited to see if it was a formal gathering. Or if it had to do with the fact that this Tremere was a Harpy and had invested interest in giving a good show to the city's vampires. He just leave the table.<br /> <br /> So I love the way the five clans of Requiem can be a lot more versatyle. I don't think, for instance, that a rock singer who turns into Mekhet will become less showy in his music. He can be as showy as ever. Maybe one day he will be the star that vanishes as long as leaves the lights, but during his performance he have absolutely no reason to step aside from the spotlight. Eventualy his mastery of Obfuscate will change how he do things, but not how he do ALL things. Or he can do precisely that, not because he's a Mekhet, but because that how THIS Mekhet took to the Curse.<br /> <br /> The most violent NPC in a game I run is a Daeva. She's passionate, for sure. She tends to become obsessed with people easily. And she grew to be very carefull about who she puts in her life. Her main blooddoll and Ghoul is currently her best friend, the other being her boyfriend (they're both Touchstones for her). But she's an elder that took centuries to learn how to deal with the clan weakness in an adaptative manner. She's Ordo Dracul and a master of the Wyrm, and took Banes to be able to dish and suffer heinous amounts of violence without risking Humanity. She's not an artist nor a prime socialite, tough she CAN use Majesty and her own looks to play the part. She's first and foremost a physical hunter.<br /> <br /> And when I look to the character, I can't see her as Gangrel, mind you. She's Daeva to the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}